A. NATURE AT THE SUN'S LIMB
   k = G M / (r c^2) = 2.123e-06; Newton's 2 k = 0.876 arcsec; Einstein's 4 k = 1.752 arcsec (Dyson, Eddington and Davidson 1920: 1.98 +- 0.16, 1.61 +- 0.40; VLBI gamma = 0.99992 +- 0.00012)
   the factor 2 over Newton: the time part (the clock's potential, g_00) and the space part (g_rr) of the weak isotropic metric, one each; Cassini fixes it to 2 x 10^-5

